{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Honor the Elders","html":"<article id='sn56.70'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 56.70 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 56.70 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>7. Paṭhamaāmakadhaññapeyyālavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>7. Abbreviated Texts on Raw Grain </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pacāyikasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Honor the Elders </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>… “Evameva kho, bhikkhave, appakā te sattā ye kule jeṭṭhāpacāyino; atha kho eteva bahutarā sattā ye kule ajeṭṭhāpacāyinoti …pe…. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“… the sentient beings who honor the elders in the family are few, while those who don’t are many. …” </span></p>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Dasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Paṭhamaāmakadhaññapeyyālavaggo sattamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Aññatra paccantaṁ paññā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Surāmerayaodakā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Matteyya petteyyā cāpi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sāmaññaṁ brahmapacāyikanti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
